---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import { buildBreadcrumbSchema } from '../../data/seo';
import { siteInfo } from '../../data/site';

const title = 'Privacy Policy | Metal 3D Powder';
const description =
  'Privacy policy for Metal 3D Powder covering inquiry data, analytics, cookies, communication records, and contact rights.';
const siteUrl = Astro.site ?? new URL('https://metal3dpowder.com');
const schema = [buildBreadcrumbSchema(siteUrl, [{ name: 'Home', path: '/' }, { name: 'Privacy' }])];
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonical="/privacy/" schema={schema}>
  <SiteHeader pathname={Astro.url.pathname} />

  <main class="page-shell content-page document-page">
    <section class="page-intro">
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
      <h1>Privacy policy for inquiry handling and website usage data.</h1>
      <p>
        Last updated: July 23, 2026. This policy covers the powder catalog, text-only online RFQ service, local
        browser storage, anti-abuse controls, website usage data, and business communication records.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="surface-card surface-card--padded rich-copy">
      <h2>Scope</h2>
      <p>
        Metal 3D Powder is operated by Suzhou Como Precision Materials Co., Ltd. (“SZComo,” “we,” or “us”).
      </p>
      <p>
        This policy applies when you browse the website, send an RFQ, request technical information, or communicate with
        SZComo through email or other business channels tied to the site.
      </p>

      <h2>Information collected</h2>
      <p>
        An online RFQ may include your name, work email, company, destination country, selected powders, per-product and
        general process, particle-size and quantity requirements, packaging, timing, and technical notes. Email
        communication may contain additional information you provide.
      </p>
      <p>
        For security and operation, the service may process IP address, request time, browser or network metadata,
        source page, a random submission reference, rate-limit results, and Cloudflare Turnstile verification data.
        Marketing-source fields such as UTM parameters or advertising click identifiers may be retained when present in
        the landing URL.
      </p>

      <h2>How information is used</h2>
      <p>
        Information is used to validate and route RFQs, review material and process fit, coordinate approved suppliers
        and service providers where necessary, prepare quotations, prevent abuse, maintain traceable communication
        records, and improve the commercial and technical usefulness of the website.
      </p>

      <h2>Browser storage, attribution, and anti-abuse controls</h2>
      <p>
        The RFQ list uses browser local storage to remember selected product IDs. A separate local record may retain the
        first and latest landing path, referring origin, and allowed campaign parameters. These records do not contain
        the technical RFQ itself and can be cleared through browser settings.
      </p>
      <p>
        The online form uses Cloudflare infrastructure for same-origin request handling, rate limiting, Turnstile
        verification, static delivery, and email routing. Anti-abuse data may be processed before an RFQ is accepted.
      </p>

      <h2>Sensitive information and separate channels</h2>
      <p>
        The online RFQ accepts text only. Do not enter export-controlled, classified, personal medical,
        customer-restricted, or other specially controlled data before an approved handling agreement is in place.
        Documents requiring special handling must use a separately arranged and approved channel.
      </p>

      <h2>Sharing, international processing, and retention</h2>
      <p>
        Information is not sold. It may be processed by website, security, and email service providers, and shared with
        approved suppliers and service providers only to the extent reasonably necessary to evaluate sourcing, testing,
        documents, logistics, compliance, or quotation scope. Because inquiries may involve international supply,
        relevant data may be processed in more than one country.
      </p>
      <p>
        RFQ, quotation, and communication records are retained only as long as reasonably required for the
        project, legitimate business records, dispute handling, security, or applicable legal obligations. Retention
        varies with the project and record type.
      </p>

      <h2>Security and service limits</h2>
      <p>
        Reasonable technical and administrative safeguards are used, but no internet or email transmission can be
        guaranteed completely secure. A successful on-screen reference means the submission service accepted the RFQ;
        it is not a quotation or proof of technical feasibility, source availability, or document acceptance.
      </p>

      <h2>Your choices</h2>
      <p>
        You may request access, correction, or deletion of inquiry data where legally applicable. You can also clear the
        RFQ list and attribution record through browser storage settings. Privacy-related requests can be sent to
        <a class="inline-link" href={`mailto:${siteInfo.email}`}>{siteInfo.email}</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>

  <SiteFooter />
</BaseLayout>
